Extensor - Article: Has Project Become a Dirty Word? If HR is really =
interested in reducing absenteeism one measures attendance. Yet the =
reality          is that many of us assign far too much importance to =
short-term tasks          rather than long-term priorities.
As the pace          of change increases, so too does the need to plan =
ahead.
They are being paid separately for it.
The must listen to alternative points of view and value other        =
people's opinions, even if they disagree with them. We quite naturally =
see tomorrow as an extension      of today, of ongoing stability, of =
gradual trends. However, lets assume that we decide to recruit      =
externally and so need to write a brief for the HR Department or =
recruitment      agency to work from. Well, as      with any illness, =
recognising the symptoms is the first step towards treatment      and =
recovery!
Could you give me some examples about how        credibility, respect =
and fairness improve the trust? Risks have increased and the fragile =
recovery is slowing.
What is different            now is that, whereas this process once took =
centuries, today it takes            place in decades or even years.
By and large many of the larger companies either      have CRM systems =
installed or have projects underway.
This is generally more cost-effective        than training everyone at a =
certain level and invariably far more effective.
I was too busy being an executive'? Alistair Schofield is MD of Extensor.
